The rule was simple: if a regression can be caught by a machine, it should never reach a human
reviewer. Accessibility checks sit in the same gate as the type checker.

![Placeholder](../../src/assets/placeholder-2.jpg)

Every gate runs the same way locally and in CI, so a red check never surprises anyone at review
time.

![Placeholder](../../src/assets/placeholder-2.jpg)
